<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>救生艇新闻：博客——保护人类</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/</link><description></description><lastBuildDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 15:21:21 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>老龄化人群中基因表达和代谢组学的纵向动态</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/09/longitudinal-dynamics-of-gene-expression-and-metabolomics-in-an-aging-population-cohort</link><description>多组学分析提供了分子水平上的全面生理学概述，但对其时空动态的了解在人类群体中仍然有限。我们对 8 年来 335 名女性的纵向全血基因表达和代谢水平进行了分析。 5,061 个基因和 181 种代谢物的水平随着时间的推移而发生变化，个体的轨迹往往与群体水平的趋势不同。纵向可变基因显示出细胞类型特异性和衰老相关途径的富集，包括心脏代谢和神经退行性疾病。纵向轨迹进一步受到遗传、昼夜节律、季节性和环境污染物暴露的影响。综合分析揭示了广泛的静态和时变的跨组学连接。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/longitudinal-dynamics-of-gene-expression-and-metabolomics-in-an-aging-population-cohort2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 15:21:19 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/09/longitudinal-dynamics-of-gene-expression-and-metabolomics-in-an-aging-population-cohort</guid></item><item><title>幸存者分享故事，小组提高了对脑动脉瘤迹象的认识</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/09/group-raises-awareness-of-brain-aneurysm-signs-as-survivor-shares-story</link><description>&lt;img src="https://politepaul.com/fd/dtDF30237DhP.xml" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 15:06:19 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/09/group-raises-awareness-of-brain-aneurysm-signs-as-survivor-shares-story</guid></item><item><title>等离子电方法可以将二氧化碳转化为可持续的喷气燃料</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/09/plasma-electric-method-could-turn-co2-into-sustainable-jet-fuel</link><description>耶鲁大学的研究人员将等离子体和电催化相结合，将二氧化碳 (CO2) 转化为燃料、酒精和其他有价值的化学品。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/plasma-electric-method-could-turn-co2-into-sustainable-jet-fuel.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 14:51:19 GM